Route the xdg-desktop-portal color scheme to web content in FallbackLinuxUi.

Chromium 154 stopped writing the portal color scheme straight into NativeTheme
(crbug.com/536445418) and routes it through LinuxUiTheme::SetColorScheme() into
each toolkit's OsSettingsProvider. FallbackLinuxUi, used when GTK and Qt are
disabled, implemented SetColorScheme() as a no-op, so prefers-color-scheme
stayed light. Give it a minimal OsSettingsProvider fed by the portal.

Register the process-lifetime fallback in GetLinuxUiThemes() when it is first
created, just like the GTK and Qt implementations. Without registration,
DarkModeManagerLinux never calls its SetDarkTheme() or SetColorScheme(), so
the portal preference cannot reach the provider or web content.

--- a/ui/linux/linux_ui_factory.cc
+++ b/ui/linux/linux_ui_factory.cc
@@ -113,7 +113,11 @@
 }
 
 LinuxUiAndTheme* GetFallbackUi() {
-  static LinuxUiAndTheme* fallback_ui = CreateFallbackUi().release();
+  static LinuxUiAndTheme* fallback_ui = [] {
+    LinuxUiAndTheme* ui = CreateFallbackUi().release();
+    GetLinuxUiThemesImpl().push_back(ui);
+    return ui;
+  }();
   return fallback_ui;
 }
 
